      <para>
        <!--
        Six tests, <filename>
test_build_latex.py::text_latex_labels</filename>,
        <filename>test_ext_autodoc.py::test_autodoc_special_members</filename>,
        <filename>test_ext_autosummary.py::test_autosummary_generate_content_for_module_imported_members</filename>,
        <filename>test_util_docutils_sphinx_directive.py::test_sphinx_directive_parse_content_to_nodes</filename>,
        <filename>test_util_docutils_sphinx_directive.py::test_sphinx_directive_parse_text_to_nodes</filename>, and
        <filename>test_util_typing.py::test_is_invalid_builtin_class</filename>,
        are known to fail due to changes in docutils-0.22 and Python 3.14.
-->
<!--https://github.com/sphinx-doc/sphinx/issues/13945 is related to the
        autodoc failure, which is Python 3.14 related. The remainder are docutils
        related. The PR mentioned in #13945 depends on a major refactor of the
        autodoc code.-->
Four tests (of over 2400 tests) are known to fail: Three in
test_ext_autodoc.py and one in test_util_typing.py.
        

        
